🛠️ Configuration & Setup
This script relies on a separate config.py file to keep your API keys, credentials, and parameters secure.

Create a file named config.py in the same directory as your main script.

Add the following variables to config.py and replace the placeholders with your actual data:

Python
# config.py

stock_end_point = "YOUR_STOCK_API_ENDPOINT"
param_stock_price = {
    "function": "TIME_SERIES_DAILY",
    "symbol": "AAPL",
    "apikey": "YOUR_STOCK_API_KEY"
}

stock_news_endpoint = "YOUR_NEWS_API_ENDPOINT"
param_stock_news = {
    "q": "apple",
    "apiKey": "YOUR_NEWS_API_KEY"
}

symbol = "AAPL"
my_email = "your_email@gmail.com"
password = "your_app_password" # Use an App Password, not your standard email password!
⚠️ Important Note on Email Security:
If you are using Gmail, standard passwords will not work due to security restrictions. You must enable 2-Step Verification on your Google Account and generate an App Password to use in the password variable.

💻 Usage
Once your config.py is set up, simply run the main script from your terminal:

Bash
python main.py
(Replace main.py with whatever you named your script).

If the stock fluctuates by more than 10%, you will receive an email for each of the top 3 news articles explaining the shift.


